### Leaderboard Update Job Tests

@baseUrl = https://localhost:7144
@adminToken = <YOUR_ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN_HERE>

### 1. Update all users' contribution points from Leaderboard to UserProfile
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/leaderboard/update-all
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Expected Response (200 OK):
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "message": "Leaderboard update job executed successfully. All users' contribution points have been synced from Leaderboard to UserProfile."
# }

### Response Details:
# - Reads all Leaderboard entries
# - For each entry, gets the corresponding UserProfile
# - Updates UserProfile.ContributionPoints = Leaderboard.TotalPoints
# - Sets UserProfile.UpdatedAt = now
# - Persists changes to database
# - Returns count of updated users and errors

###

### 2. Update a specific user's contribution points
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/leaderboard/update/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Expected Response (200 OK):
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "message": "Leaderboard update job executed successfully for user 1. Contribution points have been synced from Leaderboard to UserProfile."
# }

### Response Details:
# - Gets Leaderboard entry for UserId = 1
# - Gets UserProfile for UserId = 1
# - Updates UserProfile.ContributionPoints = Leaderboard.TotalPoints
# - Persists changes to database
# - Returns success message

###

### Error Cases:

### Case 1: Invalid User ID (UserId <= 0)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/leaderboard/update/0
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

# Response (400 Bad Request):
# {
#   "success": false,
#   "message": "Invalid user ID"
# }

###

### Case 2: Missing Authentication
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/leaderboard/update-all

# Response (401 Unauthorized)

###

### Case 3: Non-Admin User (Customer role)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/leaderboard/update-all
Authorization: Bearer <CUSTOMER_JWT_TOKEN>

# Response (403 Forbidden)

###
